{
 "id": "2025-simonienko-urban",
 "name": "Urban Flower Meadows: Semantic Differential Emotions",
 "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli: Simonienko, Jermakowicz, Szefer, Wróbel, Suprunowicz, Cwalina & Kostro-Ambroziak (2025), \"The impact of urban flower meadows on the well-being of city dwellers provides hints for planning biophilic green spaces\", Scientific Reports 15: 31981. Participants see eleven photographs from Białystok, Poland (nine urban flower meadows, a sunflower planting and a short-cut lawn) in random order and rate each on the paper's seven positive-negative pairs (joyful-sad, calm-disturbing, safe-dangerous, interesting-boring, refreshing-tiring, comfortable-uncomfortable, natural-artificial) on a 10-point scale, then give place of origin and current residence in the paper's four settlement-size groups, age and gender. Photos are those printed in the paper's Figure 1 (CC BY 4.0). Analysis as in the paper: PCA of the seven pairs into one emotion gradient, then a mixed model with respondent as random effect, meadow traits (flower colours, yellow share, green share, alien species) and rural vs city origin x residence. Differences from the original study: (1) ten numbered buttons instead of a continuous line; (2) photos are cropped from the figure, about 200 x 195 px, with the panel numbers cut off; (3) age is asked as a number instead of five groups; (4) English wording instead of Polish; the paper's top settlement group reads \"> 25,000\", taken here as more than 250,000.",
